{"abstract":"In this paper, we consider the maximum $k$-edge-colorable subgraph problem. In this problem we are given a graph $G$ and a positive integer $k$, the goal is to take $k$ matchings of $G$ such that their union contains maximum number of edges. This problem is NP-hard in cubic graphs, and polynomial-time solvable in bipartite graphs as we observe in our paper. We present an NP-hardness result for a version of this problem where we have color constraints on vertices. In fact, we show that this version is NP-hard already in bipartite graphs of maximum degree three. In order to achieve the result, we establish a connection between our problem and the problem of construction of special maximum matchings considered in the Master thesis of the author and defended back in 2003.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"2409.15388","authors":["Vahan Mkrtchyan"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-21T05:52:28+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.15388.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":15,"pdf_bytes":447153,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"7ab38dddb09bc60ef148075f764ed37ccedcc7caf68e4a2708287877b42fefa9","created_at":"2026-08-21T05:52:28+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"05cecf3f840c0bfd06d10ad7d1d9986e0e6e3492e18cacd9fcf95165bdc235c2","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"An NP-hardness result for the colored constrained maximum 2-edge-colorable subgraph problem in bipartite graphs","updated_at":"2026-08-21T05:52:28+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-675921455269","year":2024}
